1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,548
If you have a graphics card, check which port your monitor is plugged into.

2
00:00:04,828 --> 00:00:06,531
A lot of people get this wrong.

3
00:00:07,281 --> 00:00:09,836
Your PC has two sets of video ports.

4
00:00:10,116 --> 00:00:13,574
One set is on the motherboard, near the USB ports.

5
00:00:13,854 --> 00:00:17,248
The other is lower down, on the graphics card itself.

6
00:00:17,998 --> 00:00:23,345
The motherboard ports come from the processor's built-in graphics, not your graphics card.

7
00:00:23,625 --> 00:00:28,525
And if your processor has no built-in graphics, those ports may not work at all.

8
00:00:29,275 --> 00:00:37,594
Plug into the motherboard, and your expensive graphics card can end up sitting idle while games run on much weaker built-in graphics.

9
00:00:38,344 --> 00:00:39,680
So follow the cable.

10
00:00:39,960 --> 00:00:44,056
It should go into the graphics card, lower down on the back of the case.

11
00:00:44,336 --> 00:00:46,902
More PC hardware explained on the channel.

